.TH ZAREAD 1  2026-08-12 "Version 2.0.3"
.SH NAME
zaread - lightweight document converter that outputs PDF to stdout
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zaread
.BR -t \ <type>
.RB [ -v ]
.RB [ -f ]
.RB [ -c ]
.RB [ -V ]
.RB [ -h ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zaread
reads a document from stdin, converts it to PDF, and outputs the PDF to stdout.
Cached results are used when avaiable.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -v
Enable verbose output.
.br
Overwrites
.B ZA_VERBOSE
and sets it to "1".
.TP
.BR -f
Force re-conversion, ignoring any cached result.
.br
Overwrites
.B ZA_FORCE
and sets it to "1".
.TP
.BR -c
Clear the conversion cache.
.TP
.BR -V
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR -t \ <type>
Specify the input type. This is the only required flag.
.br
Supported values:
.B pdf, epub, mobi, md, typ, docx, xlsx, pptx, doc, xls, ppt, odt, ods, odp, rtf, csv
.TP
.SH ENVIRONMENT

.SS Converters
.TP
.B ZA_OFFICE_CMD
Formats:
.B ODT, ODS, ODP, CSV, RTF, DOCX, XLSX, PPTX, DOCM, XLSM, PPTM, DOC, XLS, PPT, XLSB, PPSX, DOTX
.br
Default:
.B soffice
.TP
.B ZA_OFFICE_ARG
Additional arguments passed to
.RB ZA_OFFICE_CMD .
.TP
.B ZA_MOBI_CMD
Formats:
.B MOBI
.br
Default:
.B ebook-convert
.TP
.B ZA_MOBI_ARG
Additional arguments passed to
.RB ZA_MOBI_CMD .
.TP
.B ZA_MD_CMD
Formats:
.B MD
.br
Default:
.B md2pdf
.TP
.B ZA_MD_ARG
Additional arguments passed to
.RB ZA_MD_CMD .
.TP
.B ZA_TYPST_CMD
Formats:
.B TYP
.br
Default:
.B typst
.TP
.B ZA_TYPST_ARG
Additional arguments passed to
.RB ZA_TYPST_CMD .
.br
Default:
.B compile

.SS Behavior
.TP
.B ZA_VERBOSE
Enable verbose output.
.br
Supported values:
.B 1, 0
.br
Default:
.B 0
.TP
.B ZA_FORCE
Force re-conversion instead of using cached results.
.br
Supported values:
.B 1, 0
.br
Default:
.B 0

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Usage error, missing stdin, or missing dependency.
.TP
.B 2
Unsupported file format.
.TP
.B 3
Document conversion failed.
